@startuml CCastle Renderer - current vs proposed split

skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #424242

title Where sub-visitors could further reduce the 304-line Renderer

rectangle "NOW: one big Renderer" #FFCDD2 {
  component "Renderer\n(all visit_* together)" as now
  note bottom of now
    Declarations, statements, calls,
    literals, IDs, events -- all mixed
    in a single 304-line class.
  end note
}

rectangle "PROPOSED: split along AIGR sub-packages" #C8E6C9 {
  component "Renderer\n(orchestrator only)" as core
  component "StructureRenderer\ninterfaces / protocols /\ncomponents / dispatch-tables" as struct
  component "StatementRenderer\nBody / VoidCall / If / Become" as stmt
  component "ExprRenderer\noperators (Add, Sub, And, ...)\ncalls" as expr
  component "LiteralRenderer\n_literal / fString / Constant" as lit

  core --> struct
  core --> stmt
  core --> expr
  core --> lit
}

now ==> core : refactor

note as N1
  The AIGR package is ALREADY organised as
  base / interfaces / protocols / statements /
  expressions / components.
  Mirroring that split in the writer keeps the
  "where does visit_X live?" question trivial.
end note

N1 .. struct

legend bottom
  Existing helpers (Walker, Portray, IDRef, Machinery) handle
  traversal, naming, reference-resolution and strategy.
  The proposed split addresses the *rendering* concern itself.
endlegend

@enduml
